Z||000000||MODIFIE||11-30-2001||03:21 AM||||I got this email to day ,if i am right the duke can not take no more than 7Ibs of boost also regarding the head gasket blowing in this email I got i have read that the block and the head can be machined to take some thing like a O ring seal for each cylinder for those engines that produce very high compression to keep from blowing the head gasket. Have any of you know any thing of this?<P><BR>Started out with an 87 tech4 with a intercooled (RX7 intercooler) T3 on a modified stock manifold at 160 h.p @ 10lbs of boost. Upgraded clutch and pressure plate from Broward Clutch. Intake and exhaust on heads ported to max (JB weld hole from porting), valves springs shimmed 0.060" for 6000rpm performance, inline 40 psi fuel pump, modified 52mm throttle body and reworked fuel bowl. 30 psi and above for fuel with boost pressure regulator. ARP 10mm bolts to try to cure a nasty habit of blowing head gaskets ( no luck). Changed to 88 tech4 fiero after blown transmission, constructed turbo header manifold, ugraded inline fuel pump, accel coils, and added a T4/T3 hybrid turbo. Bottom survives about 275+h.p @ 20lbs of boost but head gasket lasts only one run. Seems like only 10lbs of boost is reliable for this car. Preferred the 87 torque without the balance shafts but the 88 revs higher reliably. Good car but head gasket sucks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MR2KLR||11-30-2001||07:37 AM||||My tubo duke went thorugh 4 head gaskets in 3 weeks. water got in the oil and ate up the main brgs. dead horse now<P>84 duke<BR>Totaly stock<BR>alterd exhaust manifold<BR>TDO3 (I think) (Typhoon/Cyclone)<BR>boost gauge<P>No boost control other than stock wasted gate. BTW I got 100 miles on it in those 3-weeks<P>GOOD LUCK!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
